## Silero VAD

`core/assets/silero_vad.onnx` — the model that decides whether a piece
of audio is speech.

- Source: https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
  (file `src/silero_vad/data/silero_vad.onnx` on `master`)
- Version: 6.2.1 (the version the source project was at)
- Retrieved: 2026-08-23
- sha256: 1a153a22f4509e292a94e67d6f9b85e8deb25b4988682b7e174c65279d8788e3
- Licence: MIT

The file keeps the name it has upstream. A version in the name would
not say what matters: another project ships a model of the same version
under a similar name, with a different shape entirely. The checksum
above, and the test that asserts the model's inputs and outputs, are
what actually identify it.

